+ * layout, with 0x04 0x07 in bytes 4 and 5, as titles' own display buffers
+ * carry them (AnyPS5 PR #5697); 0x22 in byte 3 puts red in the low bits, as
+ * for the 8-bit formats. Registration took both on a console set to HDR "On
+ * when supported", which keeps its output in HDR10 and shows PQ buffers as
+ * such (LostOdysseyRecomp ps5_video_probe.cpp, 2026-10-25). */
+#define PS5_VIDEO_OUT_PIXEL_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_PQ UINT64_C(0x8100070422000000)
+#define PS5_VIDEO_OUT_PIXEL_FORMAT_A2R10G10B10_PQ UINT64_C(0x8100070400000000)
